Code copied or adapted from other projects is listed below with its source,
copyright and licence.

  CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is adapted from the Contributor Covenant, version 2.1,
  https://www.contributor-covenant.org, licensed under CC BY 4.0.

  OTLP log messages (TypeScript, Rust, Java). The ExportLogsServiceRequest /
  ExportLogsServiceResponse messages of the OTLP/gRPC LogsService are
  hand-encoded from the field numbers and types of the OpenTelemetry protocol
  definitions (opentelemetry-proto, opentelemetry/proto/collector/logs/v1,
  logs/v1, common/v1, resource/v1):
    https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-proto
    Copyright The OpenTelemetry Authors, licensed under the Apache License,
    Version 2.0.
  google.rpc.Status (decoded from gRPC error details) follows the Google APIs
  common protos (Copyright Google LLC, Apache-2.0). No code was copied from
  these projects. Go uses the generated go.opentelemetry.io/proto/otlp package
  and Python the opentelemetry-proto package instead (both Apache-2.0).

  GELF. The message format and the UDP chunking header follow the public GELF
  1.1 specification published by Graylog, Inc.
  (https://go2docs.graylog.org/current/getting_in_log_data/gelf.html); no
  Graylog code was copied.

  Notable runtime dependencies of the service code:
    TypeScript: undici (MIT), @opentelemetry/api (Apache-2.0); OTLP/gRPC uses
      node:http2 (no extra dependency).
    Rust: reqwest (MIT OR Apache-2.0, HTTP/2 for OTLP/gRPC), rustls and
      tokio-rustls (Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT, GELF TCP TLS), flate2 (MIT OR
      Apache-2.0).
    Go: google.golang.org/grpc (Apache-2.0), go.opentelemetry.io/proto/otlp
      (Apache-2.0), google.golang.org/protobuf (BSD-3-Clause).
    Python: httpx (BSD-3-Clause); the optional extra "otlp" adds grpcio
      (Apache-2.0).
    Java: com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp-jvm 5.5.0 (Apache-2.0) for OTLP/gRPC over
      HTTP/2, with its dependencies com.squareup.okio:okio (Apache-2.0) and
      org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib (Apache-2.0); Jackson (Apache-2.0).
